      {
        "id": 265561,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-05-31T15:08:20.029Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Our bi-weekly group (playing Sentinels since 2012, when we transitioned from playing Magic) has been reinvigorated by DE.</p>\n<p>Personally, I know of only one person who was unhappy about OblivAeon ending the original game, and they’ve never been willing to explain to me why they’re so mad about it. I honestly don’t understand why people are upset about that one! <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/confused.png?v=12\" title=\":confused:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":confused:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>For everyone else I know, DE has gone over great. Obviously, we’re both just presenting anecdotal accounts, but I think it is interesting that there’s such a diversity of views on this. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/thinking.png?v=12\" title=\":thinking:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":thinking:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>I have to admit to being frustrated at the distractions that have pulled them away from the RPG, even before FRG shut them down. I understand that, though, as — I’m guessing — the RPG was never going to make as much money as the board games do (especially when most of the RPG money was already made on the crowd funder). But it’s still frustrating. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/pensive.png?v=12\" title=\":pensive:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":pensive:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> Especially when the second book (Guise) was virtually useless for the kinds of games I’d run…</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2026-05-31T15:08:20.029Z",
